[{"id":"w4-predict-pos","itemId":"four-bit-weights","role":"warmup","promptHtml":"Lesson 12.1's <code class=\"nobreak\">mac4</code> with the bias −3. At each rising edge where <code class=\"nobreak\">valid</code> is 1, <code class=\"nobreak\">acc</code> takes <code class=\"nobreak\">act</code> times <code class=\"nobreak\">w</code>, added to the bias when <code class=\"nobreak\">first</code> is 1 and to the sum so far when it is 0. <code class=\"nobreak\">pos</code> is 1 while <code class=\"nobreak\">acc</code> is more than 0. Cycles 0 and 1 are drawn for you. Set <code class=\"nobreak\">pos</code> for the rest.","explanationHtml":"<p>Each product joins the sum at the edge after it is set, so <code class=\"nobreak\">pos</code> follows a cycle later. The first sum is −3 + 2 × 1 = −1: 0 in cycle 1. Adding 1 × 3 and 1 × 1 makes 2 and 3: 1 in cycles 2 and 3. Then <code class=\"nobreak\">first</code> starts a new sum, −3 + 1 × 2 = −1: 0 in cycle 4. Adding 2 × 1 makes 1, 6 × 0 adds nothing, and 1 × 4 makes 5: 1 from cycle 5 on, and <code class=\"nobreak\">acc</code> keeps its 5 while <code class=\"nobreak\">valid</code> is 0.</p>","type":"waveform","wave":{"id":"w4-pos","source":"hdl/level-12/mac4/mac4_tb.sv","timescale":"1ps","period":10000,"periodText":"10 ns","unit":"cycle","cycles":9,"signals":[{"label":"clk","path":"mac4_tb.clk","width":1,"role":"clock","changes":[[0,"1"],[0.5,"0"],[1,"1"],[1.5,"0"],[2,"1"],[2.5,"0"],[3,"1"],[3.5,"0"],[4,"1"],[4.5,"0"],[5,"1"],[5.5,"0"],[6,"1"],[6.5,"0"],[7,"1"],[7.5,"0"],[8,"1"],[8.5,"0"]]},{"label":"valid","path":"mac4_tb.valid","width":1,"role":"signal","changes":[[0,"1"],[7.5,"0"]]},{"label":"first","path":"mac4_tb.first","width":1,"role":"signal","changes":[[0,"1"],[1.5,"0"],[3.5,"1"],[4.5,"0"]]},{"label":"act[7:0]","path":"mac4_tb.act","width":8,"role":"signal","changes":[[0,"00000000"],[0.5,"00000010"],[1.5,"00000001"],[4.5,"00000010"],[5.5,"00000110"],[6.5,"00000001"],[7.5,"00000000"]]},{"label":"w[3:0]","path":"mac4_tb.w","width":4,"role":"signal","changes":[[0,"0000"],[0.5,"0001"],[1.5,"0011"],[2.5,"0001"],[3.5,"0010"],[4.5,"0001"],[5.5,"0000"],[6.5,"0100"],[7.5,"0000"]]},{"label":"pos","path":"mac4_tb.pos","width":1,"role":"signal","changes":[[0,"0"],[2,"1"],[4,"0"],[5,"1"]],"samples":["0","0","1","1","0","1","1","1","1"]}]},"answer":"pos","prefill":[0,1]},{"id":"w4-predict-neg","itemId":"four-bit-weights","role":"core","promptHtml":"Lesson 12.1's <code class=\"nobreak\">mac4</code> with the bias 5 and some negative weights. At each rising edge where <code class=\"nobreak\">valid</code> is 1, <code class=\"nobreak\">acc</code> takes <code class=\"nobreak\">act</code> times <code class=\"nobreak\">w</code>, added to the bias when <code class=\"nobreak\">first</code> is 1 and to the sum so far when it is 0. <code class=\"nobreak\">pos</code> is 1 while <code class=\"nobreak\">acc</code> is more than 0. <code class=\"nobreak\">w</code> is drawn in hexadecimal: E is 1110, which as a signed 4-bit number is −2. In cycle 0, <code class=\"nobreak\">pos</code> is still 1 from the sum before. Set <code class=\"nobreak\">pos</code> for every cycle.","explanationHtml":"<p>As signed numbers, E is −2, F is −1 and 8 is −8. The sums are 5 + 2 × −2 = 1, then 1 − 3 = −2, −2 + 4 = 2, 2 − 8 = −6, −6 + 8 = 2 and 2 − 8 = −6, so <code class=\"nobreak\">pos</code> is 1, 0, 1, 0, 1, 0 in cycles 1 to 6. A new sum starts from 5: 5 − 3 = 2, then 2 + 9 = 11, so 1 in cycles 7 to 9. Read as unsigned, E would count as 14, and no sum here would be negative.</p>","type":"waveform","wave":{"id":"w4-neg","source":"hdl/level-12/mac4/mac4_tb.sv","timescale":"1ps","period":10000,"periodText":"10 ns","unit":"cycle","cycles":10,"signals":[{"label":"clk","path":"mac4_tb.clk","width":1,"role":"clock","changes":[[0,"1"],[0.5,"0"],[1,"1"],[1.5,"0"],[2,"1"],[2.5,"0"],[3,"1"],[3.5,"0"],[4,"1"],[4.5,"0"],[5,"1"],[5.5,"0"],[6,"1"],[6.5,"0"],[7,"1"],[7.5,"0"],[8,"1"],[8.5,"0"],[9,"1"],[9.5,"0"]]},{"label":"valid","path":"mac4_tb.valid","width":1,"role":"signal","changes":[[0,"0"],[0.5,"1"],[8.5,"0"],[9.5,"1"]]},{"label":"first","path":"mac4_tb.first","width":1,"role":"signal","changes":[[0,"0"],[0.5,"1"],[1.5,"0"],[6.5,"1"],[7.5,"0"],[9.5,"1"]]},{"label":"act[7:0]","path":"mac4_tb.act","width":8,"role":"signal","changes":[[0,"00000000"],[0.5,"00000010"],[1.5,"00000011"],[2.5,"00000001"],[3.5,"00000100"],[4.5,"00001000"],[5.5,"00000001"],[6.5,"00000011"],[7.5,"00001001"],[8.5,"00000000"]]},{"label":"w[3:0]","path":"mac4_tb.w","width":4,"role":"signal","changes":[[0,"0000"],[0.5,"1110"],[1.5,"1111"],[2.5,"0100"],[3.5,"1110"],[4.5,"0001"],[5.5,"1000"],[6.5,"1111"],[7.5,"0001"],[8.5,"0000"],[9.5,"1000"]]},{"label":"pos","path":"mac4_tb.pos","width":1,"role":"signal","changes":[[0,"1"],[2,"0"],[3,"1"],[4,"0"],[5,"1"],[6,"0"],[7,"1"]],"samples":["1","1","0","1","0","1","0","1","1","1"]}]},"answer":"pos"},{"id":"w4-find-bug","itemId":"four-bit-weights","role":"stretch","promptHtml":"<code class=\"nobreak\">mac4_bug</code> should give the same sums as lesson 12.1's <code class=\"nobreak\">mac4</code>. Its testbench passes the sums whose weights are 0 to 7, then fails at the first negative weight: from the bias 5, with <code class=\"nobreak\">act</code> 2 and <code class=\"nobreak\">w</code> −2, <code class=\"nobreak\">acc</code> becomes 33 instead of 1. Pick the line that is wrong.","explanationHtml":"<p>The weight port is not declared <code class=\"nobreak\">signed</code>. One unsigned operand makes the whole product unsigned, so 1110 counts as 14: 2 × 14 = 28, and 5 + 28 = 33. Declared <code class=\"nobreak\">signed</code>, it is −2, and the sum is 5 − 4 = 1. The two agree for the weights 0 to 7, which is why the first sums pass. Writing <code class=\"nobreak\">$signed(w)</code> in the product would also work, but the weight is −8 to 7 everywhere, so its port is where its type belongs.</p>","type":"find-bug","file":"hdl/level-12/mac4_bug/mac4_bug.sv","firstLine":1,"lines":[[{"text":"// One lane of the 3D decoder's hidden engines, in small: an 8-bit","color":"var(--code-token-comment)","bold":false}],[{"text":"// activation, never negative, times a 4-bit signed weight, from -8 to 7,","color":"var(--code-token-comment)","bold":false}],[{"text":"// one product a cycle, added up from the bias. The activation is made a","color":"var(--code-token-comment)","bold":false}],[{"text":"// signed number with a 0 on top before the product: in SystemVerilog, if","color":"var(--code-token-comment)","bold":false}],[{"text":"// one operand of an expression is unsigned, the whole expression is","color":"var(--code-token-comment)","bold":false}],[{"text":"// worked out unsigned, and a weight of -1 would count as 15.","color":"var(--code-token-comment)","bold":false}],[{"text":"module","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"mac4_bug","color":"var(--code-token-function)","bold":false},{"text":" (","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}],[{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"input","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":true},{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"logic","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":"               clk,","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}],[{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"input","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":true},{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"logic","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":"               valid,      ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"// act * w is a product to add","color":"var(--code-token-comment)","bold":false}],[{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"input","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":true},{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"logic","color":"var(--c